avcodec/mediacodecdec: make H.264's codec again when the SPS changes the size

goffmpeg #101. Upstream: not submitted yet.

h264_mediacodec configures MediaCodec once, with the first SPS and PPS,
and sends every packet after to that codec, a new SPS included. Some
decoders carry on through a resolution change; MediaTek's does not.
Measured on a moto g power 2024 (Android 14), goffmpeg's
sample_size_change.ts (MPEG-TS, 320x240 then 640x360) gives 5 of its 35
frames and none after the change, where a OnePlus Pad 2 and a Pixel 9a
give all 35.

A packet whose SPS describes a picture of another size than the codec's
is now held. The codec is drained, the frames of the old size come out,
and a new codec is made for the packet's SPS and PPS, which then get the
packet. A repeated SPS of the same size, as MPEG-TS sends one with every
IDR, changes nothing.

